# Project setup

- Godot 4 source. Build: `scons -j14 target=editor tests=yes vulkan=no accesskit=no angle=no`
- Headless tests: `./bin/godot.macos.editor.arm64 --headless --test`
- MoltenVK is not installed on this machine; Metal is enough. Never switch to `vulkan=yes`.

# Architecture — bound global APIs

- Implementation: `core/math/math_funcs.h` — follow `smoothstep` as the canonical pattern.
- Binding: `core/variant/variant_utility.h` + `core/variant/variant_utility.cpp` (`register_utility_function`).
- Docs: `doc/classes/@GlobalScope.xml` — keep entries alphabetical like their neighbors.
- Tests: `tests/core/math/test_math_funcs.cpp`.
- A new global function touches all four surfaces in one change. No partial landings.

# Workflow

- Rebuild after C++ changes before claiming anything works.
- Verify with a headless binding check (`--headless --script`), not just a successful compile.
- Call out anything that still needs eyes in the running editor in the final response.